  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Academy teaching places humans above all creatures, and Gu as the essence of heaven and earth.",
      "chapters": [
        7
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "academy-teaching",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu Master attire at rank one means leaving mortal life and entering the middle class of the entire human race; even rank one is the bottom of that tier, and mortals must give way.",
      "chapters": [
        87
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "academy-teaching",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Beast tides make it hard for humanity to survive. Humans need resources and living space, no different from wild beasts and insects.",
      "chapters": [
        93
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "academy-teaching",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_beast_tide"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Apart from the humans born from Ren Zu’s proper bloodline, there were also variant humans. Variant humans may be more intelligent than other lifeforms, but they are far from having human wisdom: hairy men were ignorant, eggmen were innocent, and stonemen were naive and barbaric. Man is the spirit of all living beings.",
      "chapters": [
        424
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "proper-bloodline",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ren_zu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Humans have the highest intelligence and complex thoughts. Variant humans have lower intelligence and purer minds, and their groups are more united than humans. Humans ruled the five regions and were the strongest. Variant humans were ostracized and suppressed, and variant human slaves were sold in the market in every region. Among the races, humans held absolute dominance.",
      "chapters": [
        866
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "present-standing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "During the Immemorial Antiquity Era and the Remote Antiquity Era, variant humans were in control of most of the world. Even with Ren Zu, his ten children, Primordial Origin Immortal Venerable, and Star Constellation Immortal Venerable, there were very few humans in the world.",
      "chapters": [
        871
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "antiquity-numbers",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "evt_era_immemorial",
        "evt_era_remote",
        "char_primordial_origin_immortal_venerable",
        "char_star_constellation_immortal_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "During the Remote Antiquity Era, Primordial Origin Immortal Venerable and Star Constellation Immortal Venerable appeared, leading humans to resist the rule of variant humans and establishing the authority of humans. By the Olden Antiquity Era, three human Demon Venerables appeared, creating wars and exterminating the beastmen race, stabilizing humans as the rulers.",
      "chapters": [
        912
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "venerable-leadership",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "evt_era_olden"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "There were ten variant human races in the Gu world: hairy men, rockmen, snowmen, feathermen, mermen, inkmen, eggmen, beastmen, miniman, and mushroommen. Humans’ intelligence is too high, and they expend too many resources to raise.",
      "chapters": [
        1489
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "variant-races",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
